+**Parameters**
+- **Input Resolution:** $512 \times 512$ pixels [S1, unofficial].
+- **Overlap Thresholds:** $\phi$ and $\psi$ control the minimum overlap between context and target images. Typical values tested: Close $(0.9, 0.9)$, Medium $(0.7, 0.7)$, Wide $(0.5, 0.5)$, Very Wide $(0.3, 0.3)$ [S1, unofficial].
+- **Color Parameterization:** Constant, view-independent color $S \in \mathbb{R}^3$ is used in experiments, with ablation for view-dependent spherical harmonics [S1, unofficial].
+- **Activation Functions:** Normalization for quaternions, exponential for scales and offsets, sigmoid for opacities [S1, unofficial].
+
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
+- **Extrapolation:** Supervising rendering loss for pixels not visible in context views (obscured or outside frustums) is counterproductive. The loss masking strategy is critical to prevent this [S1, unofficial].
+- **Local Minima:** Unlike methods that predict depth distributions, Splatt3R directly supervises positions using ground-truth point clouds, providing a monotonic loss path to the correct location [S1, unofficial].
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The method is feed-forward, requiring a single forward pass through the network for inference. It achieves reconstruction at 4 FPS for $512 \times 512$ resolution [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Memory usage is proportional to the number of pixels in the input images, as it predicts per-pixel Gaussians. The number of Gaussians is $2 \times H \times W$ (union of both images) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** On ScanNet++ test scenes, Splatt3R achieves PSNR 19.66, SSIM 0.757, and LPIPS 0.234 for the "Close" view overlap setting ($\phi=0.9, \psi=0.9$) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:**
-    *   Does not require camera intrinsics, extrinsics, or depth maps [S1, unofficial].
-    *   Generalizes to uncalibrated, in-the-wild images [S1, unofficial].
-    *   Can extrapolate to viewpoints beyond the stereo baseline [S1, unofficial].
-    *   Real-time rendering of predicted splats [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:**
-    *   Performance degrades with wider baselines (lower $\phi, \psi$) [S1, unofficial].
-    *   Relies on the quality of the frozen MASt3R backbone for geometry [S1, unofficial].
-    *   Training requires ground truth depth and poses for loss masking, which are not available at inference [S1, unofficial].
+- **Time Complexity:** Inference is a single forward pass, achieving 4 FPS at $512 \times 512$ resolution [S1, unofficial].
